— 🇺🇸/🇷🇺 BREAKING: U.S. President Donald Trump says Russia has agreed to immediately supply more than 300,000 tons of diesel fuel to U.S. and global markets, followed by another 500,000 tons in November and one million tons shortly afterward.

Trump said Russia would later provide an additional three million tons of diesel, adding that the agreement, together with U.S. control over the Strait of Hormuz, would help drive fuel prices lower.

